    "problemStatement": "For an array AAA of length NNN, an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N) is called a prefix maxima if and only if:\n\nAi≥Aj&nbsp;for&nbsp;every&nbsp;j≤iA_i \\ge A_j \\text{ for every } j \\le iAi​≥Aj​&nbsp;for&nbsp;every&nbsp;j≤iWe define a function PMXPMXPMX as follows:\n\n\nLet PPP be the set of all prefix maximas of AAA.\nThen, PMX(A)=⨁X∈PAX\\text{PMX}(A) = \\bigoplus_{X \\in P} A_XPMX(A)=⨁X∈P​AX​\nwhere ⨁\\bigoplus⨁ denotes the bitwise XOR operation.\n\nThat is, PMX(A)PMX(A)PMX(A) denotes the bitwise XOR of all the prefix maxima of AAA.\n\nTwo arrays AAA and BBB of length NNN are said to be distinct if there exists at least one index iii  (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N) such that Ai≠BiA_i \\neq B_iAi​=Bi​.\n\nYou are given an array AAA of length NNN.\n\nLet SSS be the set of all rearrangements of AAA, without duplicates.\n\nFor example, if A=[1,1,2]A = [1, 1, 2]A=[1,1,2], then S={[1,1,2],[1,2,1],[2,1,1]}S = \\{[1, 1, 2], [1, 2, 1], [2, 1, 1]\\}S={[1,1,2],[1,2,1],[2,1,1]}.\n\nYour task is to compute the expected value of PMX(B)PMX(B)PMX(B) across all arrays B∈SB\\in SB∈S.\n\nOutput the result modulo 998 244 353†998\\,244\\,353^\\dagger998244353†.\n\n†^\\dagger† Formally, let M=998 244 353M = 998\\,244\\,353M=998244353. It can be shown that the answer can be expressed as an irreducible fraction pq\\frac{p}{q}qp​, where ppp and qqq are integers and q≢0(modM)q \\not \\equiv 0 \\pmod{M}q≡0(modM). Output the integer equal to p⋅q−1 mod Mp \\cdot q^{-1} \\bmod Mp⋅q−1modM. In other words, output such an integer xxx that 0≤x&lt;M0 \\le x &lt; M0≤x&lt;M and x⋅q≡p(modM)x \\cdot q \\equiv p \\pmod{M}x⋅q≡p(modM).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the size of array AAA.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the expected value of PMX(B)PMX(B)PMX(B) across all distinct rearrangements of AAA, modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10610^6106."
    ],
