        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: For A=[1,1,1]A = [1, 1, 1]A=[1,1,1], the only rearrangement is AAA itself.\nWe have PMX([1,1,1])=1⊕1⊕1=1PMX([1, 1, 1]) = 1\\oplus 1\\oplus 1 = 1PMX([1,1,1])=1⊕1⊕1=1, so the answer is 111.\nTest case 222: For A=[1,2]A = [1, 2]A=[1,2], we have the following rearrangements:\n\n[1,2][1, 2][1,2], for which PMX([1,2])=1⊕2=3PMX([1, 2]) = 1\\oplus 2 = 3PMX([1,2])=1⊕2=3.\n[2,1][2, 1][2,1], for which PMX([2,1])=2PMX([2, 1]) = 2PMX([2,1])=2.\n\nThe expected value is hence\n12⋅(3+2)=52\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (3 + 2) = \\frac{5}{2}21​⋅(3+2)=25​\nIt can be verified that this is 2⋅499122179≡5(mod998244353)2\\cdot 499122179 \\equiv 5 \\pmod {998244353}2⋅499122179≡5(mod998244353)."
